# GUIShop Statistics System

GUIShop tracks player shop activity and exposes it via PlaceholderAPI and a Java API.

## Key Classes

### Statistics Package (`src/com/pablo67340/guishop/statistics/`)
- `PlayerStats.java` - Data class holding a player's statistics
- `StatisticsManager.java` - SQLite storage + caching
- `GUIShopPlaceholderExpansion.java` - PlaceholderAPI integration

## Database Storage

SQLite: `plugins/GUIShop/Data/player_statistics.db`

### Tables

```sql
-- Player aggregate stats
CREATE TABLE player_stats (
    uuid TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
    total_spent REAL DEFAULT 0,
    total_earned REAL DEFAULT 0,
    items_bought INTEGER DEFAULT 0,
    items_sold INTEGER DEFAULT 0
);

-- Individual transactions (for top items)
CREATE TABLE item_transactions (
    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
    uuid TEXT,
    material TEXT,
    quantity INTEGER,
    price REAL,
    type TEXT,  -- 'BUY' or 'SELL'
    timestamp INTEGER
);
```

## Recording Transactions

### In Shop.java (command items):
```java
StatisticsManager.getInstance().recordPurchase(player, material, 1, price);
```

### In Quantity.java (regular purchases):
```java
StatisticsManager.getInstance().recordPurchase(player, item.getMaterial(), quantity, pricePaid);
```

### In Sell.java:
```java
StatisticsManager.getInstance().recordSale(player, material, quantity, priceEarned);
```

## Cache Management

Like economy, online players have stats cached:
```java
// In PlayerListener:
StatisticsManager.getInstance().loadPlayerCache(player);   // on join
StatisticsManager.getInstance().unloadPlayerCache(player); // on quit
```

## Singleton Access

```java
StatisticsManager.getInstance()
PlayerStats stats = StatisticsManager.getInstance().getStats(uuid);
```

## PlaceholderAPI Placeholders

All prefixed with `%guishop_`:

| Placeholder | Description |
|-------------|-------------|
| `total_spent` | Money spent (with commas) |
| `total_spent_raw` | Money spent (raw number) |
| `total_spent_formatted` | Money spent (abbreviated: 1.5M) |
| `total_earned` | Money earned (with commas) |
| `total_earned_raw` | Money earned (raw number) |
| `total_earned_formatted` | Money earned (abbreviated) |
| `items_bought` | Items purchased count |
| `items_bought_formatted` | Items purchased (abbreviated) |
| `items_sold` | Items sold count |
| `items_sold_formatted` | Items sold (abbreviated) |
| `top_bought_1` | #1 most bought: "Material: Qty" |
| `top_bought_1_material` | #1 material name only |
| `top_bought_1_quantity` | #1 quantity only |
| `top_bought_2`, `top_bought_3` | #2, #3 most bought |
| `top_sold_1`, `top_sold_2`, `top_sold_3` | Most sold items |

## API Methods (GUIShopAPI)

```java
GUIShopAPI.isStatisticsEnabled()
GUIShopAPI.getPlayerStats(player)
GUIShopAPI.getTotalSpent(player)
GUIShopAPI.getTotalEarned(player)
GUIShopAPI.getItemsBought(player)
GUIShopAPI.getItemsSold(player)
GUIShopAPI.getTotalSpentFormatted(player, abbreviated)
GUIShopAPI.getTopSpenders(limit)
GUIShopAPI.getTopEarners(limit)
GUIShopAPI.resetPlayerStats(player)
```

## PlayerStats Class

```java
public class PlayerStats {
    private UUID uuid;
    private BigDecimal totalSpent;
    private BigDecimal totalEarned;
    private int itemsBought;
    private int itemsSold;
    private Map<String, Integer> topBoughtItems;  // Material -> Count
    private Map<String, Integer> topSoldItems;
    
    public void addSpent(BigDecimal amount);
    public void addEarned(BigDecimal amount);
    public String getTopItem(int rank, boolean bought);
    public String getTopItemMaterial(int rank, boolean bought);
    public Integer getTopItemQuantity(int rank, boolean bought);
}
```

## Number Formatting

Uses `MathUtil` for formatting:
```java
MathUtil.formatWithCommas(amount)    // "1,234,567.89"
MathUtil.formatAbbreviated(amount)   // "1.23M"
NameUtil.formatMaterialName(mat)     // "DIAMOND_SWORD" -> "Diamond Sword"
```
